{
  "title": "calibration cohorts over trusted samples, the fallback to broader classes, and one snapshot identity on every device",
  "covers": [
    "exact records are the samples; the sparse, timing-floor and reconstructed records beneath the parent are in the population and the coverage denominators, never samples of the exact set",
    "the model dimension comes from the checkout's harness model, replicated with the attempt: the same key on the writer, the tail and a hydrated device",
    "a sample divides by its first worker attempt's estimateAtStart: e1 was re-estimated from 2h to 1h after it started and still reads 20m over 2h",
    "a full key with fewer than five samples falls back, model first: three opus and two sonnet samples both read their without_model class of five; a lone bug falls back to the whole set",
    "reconstructed history is a separate set only when asked for, with its own cohorts: two samples, below the minimum everywhere",
    "the snapshot id is the same on every device and for the cohort and sample listings, because every input is replicated",
    "samples and members list oldest resolution first, and two resolved in one millisecond by issue id: the same order on every device, and the order the cursor follows"
  ],
